  "id": "policy-analysis",
  "term": "policy analysis",
  "definition": "Policy analysis is a structured way of examining how a policy works by looking not only at its stated aims or text, but also at the surrounding context, the steps through which it is carried out, and the people involved. It is used to clarify how policy intentions relate to what actually happens in practice, especially in complex settings where priorities and implementation change over time.",
